<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Islamic State of Afghanistan</h1><p class="st-meta">1992 CE – 2001 CE · capital Kabul</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The mujahideen government that took Kabul in 1992 and fought a ruinous civil war, remaining the internationally recognised government even after the Taliban won.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-najibullah">Mohammad Najibullah's</a> government of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/democratic-republic-of-afghanistan">Democratic Republic of Afghanistan</a> in April 1992, mujahideen parties agreed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshawar">Peshawar</a> Accord to form the Islamic State of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present">Afghanistan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sibghatullah-mojaddedi">Sibghatullah Mojaddedi</a> served briefly as president, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanuddin-rabbani">Burhanuddin Rabbani</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamiat-e-islami">Jamiat-e Islami</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-massoud">Ahmad Shah Massoud</a> as defence minister, never controlled the country. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulbuddin-hekmatyar">Gulbuddin Hekmatyar's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hezb-e-islami">Hezb-e Islami</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-rashid-dostum">Abdul Rashid Dostum's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> militia and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazara">Hazara</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hezb-e-wahdat">Hezb-e Wahdat</a> fought each other and the government for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>, killing tens of thousands of civilians in shelling. Regional warlords ruled elsewhere, and the country fragmented.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Taliban took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> in 1996, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-1996-2001">Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan</a> (1996-2001). Rabbani's government kept the UN seat and controlled the north-east through the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ouetsu-reppan-domei">Northern Alliance</a>. After the US-led intervention of 2001, Rabbani handed power to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-afghanistan">Islamic Republic of Afghanistan</a>'s interim administration.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/islamic-state-of-afghanistan.jpg" alt="Islamic State of Afghanistan" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Saul ip · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Afghanistan_(1992%E2%80%932001).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1992 CE – 2001 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kabul</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sibghatullah Mojaddedi, Burhanuddin Rabbani</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pashto, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rabbani government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1996&amp;focus=islamic-state-of-afghanistan" aria-label="Islamic State of Afghanistan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6437 927 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Islamic State of Afghanistan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6757 1183L6757 1183M6757 1183L6757 1183M6757 1183L6690 1235"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6757 1183h0M6757 1183h0M6690 1235h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6757 1183h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6757 1183h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kabul. <a href="/atlas?year=1996&amp;focus=islamic-state-of-afghanistan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
